 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "Rigorous data mining means conditioning interesting results on the fact that they come from searching through data.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   2
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "Our data-mined portfolio is the simple average of the top 1% of strategies, based on EB-predicted Sharpe ratios.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   2
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "compared to the mean return of 5.9% per year found by averaging the 200 published strategies from Chen and Zimmermann (2022)",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   2
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "our strategies can be constructed using only information available in real time",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   2
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 3,
  "citation": "In essence, EB measures the distance between the empirical t-stat distribution and the standard normal null.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   3
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 3,
  "citation": "the top 20 strategies according to predicted Sharpe ratios using data available in 1993 have themes rarely seen in academic journals",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   3
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 4,
  "citation": "Our EB predictions are constructed using a simple 20-year rolling window, and thus fail to account for this break.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   4
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 4,
  "citation": "using the standard null, that the mean long-short return (or alpha) is zero",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   4
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 5,
  "citation": "Chen and Zimmermann (2020); Chen and Velikov (2022); and Jensen, Kelly, and Pedersen (2023) recommend empirical Bayes shrinkage.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   5
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 5,
  "citation": "More recently, Marrow and Nagel (2024) use empirical Bayes to study past return signals, with a focus on signal interactions and optimal weighting of more recent data.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   5
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 6,
  "citation": "A key feature of these strategies is that they are not selected based on having notable historical returns. Instead, they are constructed to systematically explore various types of data.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   6
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 6,
  "citation": "Results that mine data following Yan and Zheng (2017) and Harvey (2017) are similar and can be found in the first draft of our paper on arxiv.org or via our github site.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   6
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 6,
  "citation": "let r i be a performance measure for strategy i (e.g. mean return, alpha)",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   6
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 7,
  "citation": "provided one has a probability model for",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   7
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 7,
  "citation": "We will not use economic theory to determine the probability model, and thus our search is largely atheoretical.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   7
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 8,
  "citation": "This is a hierarchical structure, where the strategy family determines the actual performance, which in turn determines the measured performance.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   8
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 9,
  "citation": "If conditions 1 and 2 hold, then naive data mining selects the same set of strategies as empirical Bayes.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   9
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 10,
  "citation": "We select as our performance measure the t-statistic on the raw long-short return",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   10
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 10,
  "citation": "The latent performance is a mixture of two normals that depends on the strategy family",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   10
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 10,
  "citation": "using quasi-maximum likelihood",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   10
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 10,
  "citation": "This estimation is done using the past 20 years of long-short returns, separately for each “forecasting year” spanning 1983-2019.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   10
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 11,
  "citation": "Each year, we sign strategies to have positive predicted returns, and then form portfolios that equally-weight strategies in the top X % of predicted Sharpe ratios.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   11
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 11,
  "citation": "For comparison, we also examine a portfolio that equally-weighs published strategies from the Chen and Zimmermann (2022) dataset.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   11
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 11,
  "citation": "unlike the EB-mined strategies, which are formed using only information available in real-time, the published strategies contain look-ahead bias",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   11
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 12,
  "citation": "one can find long-short returns comparable to those from the best journals in finance, just by mining data, with little thought about the underlying economics",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   12
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 12,
  "citation": "Unlike the published strategy returns, our returns can be found using only information available in real-time.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   12
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 12,
  "citation": "These stylized facts offer a parsimonious description of the “factor zoo.”",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   12
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
