  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 15,
  "citation": "We then predict the mean returns for each portfolio by averaging the EB predictions",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   15
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 15,
  "citation": "This result is consistent with Chen and Zimmermann (2020), who find shrinkage of only 12% for published anomalies, which are largely equal-weighted and based on accounting variables.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   15
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 16,
  "citation": "empirical Bayes provides quantitative, accurate estimates of the precise amount of predictability",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   16
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 17,
  "citation": "theory is typically used to understand patterns found in long samples of data, spanning many decades",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   17
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 17,
  "citation": "our theory-free EB mining process",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   4,
   17
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 17,
  "citation": "An alternative approach is to use false discovery controls",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   17
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 17,
  "citation": "The ideal approach remains an unsettled question.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   17
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 17,
  "citation": "For each year and each strategy family, we apply these methods using the past 20 years of data to estimate a t-statistic hurdle.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   17
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 20,
  "citation": "can be interpreted as an estimate of the probability that a strategy is null",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   20
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 21,
  "citation": "Null strategies are, typically, those with an actual performance of zero.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   21
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 22,
  "citation": "in the standard setting where the null is that the strategy has zero long-short return or zero alpha, then the RW method tends to imply extreme conservatism",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   22
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 23,
  "citation": "Our out-of-sample tests offer an intuitive method for comparing multiple testing methods.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   23
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 24,
  "citation": "we want to ensure that our methods do not incorporate knowledge that would come from reading finance publications",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   24
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 24,
  "citation": "Earlier versions of our paper use Yan and Zheng’s method and found similar results.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   24
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 25,
  "citation": "Earlier versions of our paper used Harvey’s method and found similar results.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   25
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 26,
  "citation": "We construct the quasi-likelihood using the distr package in R (Ruckdeschel et al. (2006)) and optimize using the BOBYQA algorithm in the nloptr package",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   26
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 27,
  "citation": "does not have a stopping condition based on",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   27
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "It earns out-of-sample returns of 5.7% per year over the 1983-2020 sample",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   2
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "recent empirical evidence finds this method is ineffective, even for theories published in top finance journals (Chen, Lopez-Lira, and Zimmermann (2022))",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   2
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 4,
  "citation": "A brief explanation of why Benjamini and Yekutieli (2001) Theorem 1.3 is excessively conservative is found in Section 2.5 of Chen (2024a).",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   4
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 5,
  "citation": "We add to Yan and Zheng (2017) and Chen, Lopez-Lira, and Zimmermann (2022), who document that mining accounting data can produce substantial out-of-sample returns.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   5
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 6,
  "citation": "So unlike most datasets in asset pricing (e.g. Ken French’s size- and B/M-sorted portfolios; Chen and Zimmermann (2022)), ours is arguably free of data mining bias.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   6
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 11,
  "citation": "Over the full 1983-2020 sample, the top 1% portfolio earns 5.70% per year, compared to the 5.88% return from published strategies.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   11
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 11,
  "citation": "if we focus on strategies in top journals that were published pre-2004, the performance is very similar to the EB-mined strategies",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   11
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CHENDIM",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2311.10685/2311.10685v3.pdf",
  "empreinte": "d338d13e08302df0f5d38c8886449eebe30ebd1a20d29390757658644ec50b7e",
  "page": 15,
  "citation": "Finally, we form a portfolio that equally-weighs strategies in each group and hold for one year",
